      "<1% (systemic bioavailability of swallowed drug)", "des-CIC elimination half-life is 3.5 hours; intracellular lipid conjugation extends lung duration to 24 hours", ">99% (des-CIC)", "Improvement in lung function begins within 24 to 48 hours; peak at 2 to 4 weeks", "24 hours (can be dosed once daily in mild-to-moderate asthma)",
      ["Maintenance treatment of asthma as prophylactic therapy in adult and adolescent patients 12 years and older (Alvesco: 80 to 320 mcg once or twice daily)", "Treatment of symptoms of seasonal and perennial allergic rhinitis (Omnaris nasal spray)"],
      ["Primary treatment of status asthmaticus or acute asthma exacerbations requiring intensive measures", "Hypersensitivity to ciclesonide"],
      ["ON-SITE LUNG ACTIVATION: Inactive prodrug is activated by lung esterases; inactive in the mouth, dramatically reducing oropharyngeal candidiasis (thrush) and hoarseness compared to other inhaled steroids", "Not for acute bronchospasm rescue", "Once-daily dosing option in the evening provides 24-hour asthma control"],
      ["Headache", "Nasopharyngitis", "Sinusitis", "Upper respiratory tract infection", "Oral candidiasis (exceptionally low: <1-2%)"],
      ["Paradoxical bronchospasm (immediate)", "HPA axis suppression (only at supratherapeutic doses)", "Severe hypersensitivity / angioedema (rare)"],
      ["Strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (ketoconazole, ritonavir - increase des-CIC exposure; monitor for steroid effects)", "Zero significant interactions at recommended doses"],
      ["Asthma symptom control and FEV1/peak flows", "Adolescent growth monitoring", "Inhalation technique"],
      "Category C; use during pregnancy only if potential benefit justifies potential risk.",
