      ["250 mcg (starter pack)", "500 mcg"], ["Film-coated Tablet"], ["Oral"],
      "Selectively and competitively inhibits phosphodiesterase-4 (PDE4), the predominant cAMP-metabolizing enzyme in immune and inflammatory cells (neutrophils, macrophages, CD8+ T cells, bronchial smooth muscle); elevates intracellular cyclic AMP (cAMP), suppressing pro-inflammatory cytokine and chemokine release.",
      "Significantly reduces sputum neutrophils, decreases bronchial wall thickness, improves post-bronchodilator FEV1 (by 50-80 mL), and reduces the rate of moderate and severe COPD exacerbations by approx. 17-20% in patients with severe COPD, chronic bronchitis, and frequent flare-ups.",
      "Rapidly absorbed; peak plasma concentrations of active roflumilast N-oxide in 4 to 8 hours; absolute bioavailability approx. 80%; unaffected by food.",
      "Apparent volume of distribution approx. 2.9 L/kg; highly bound to human plasma proteins (99% for parent; 97% for active N-oxide).",
      "Extensively metabolized in the liver: converted primarily by CYP3A4 and CYP1A2 to roflumilast N-oxide (which accounts for >90% of total in vivo PDE4 inhibitory activity).",
      "Excreted predominantly in urine (approx. 70% as inactive metabolites) and faeces (approx. 20%); <1% unchanged parent drug in urine.",
      "Approximately 80%", "Parent drug: 17 hours; Active N-oxide: 30 hours (ideal for once-daily dosing)", "99%", "Clinical reduction in COPD exacerbations develops over 4 to 12 weeks", "24 hours (once daily)",
      ["Maintenance treatment to reduce the risk of COPD exacerbations in adult patients with severe COPD (FEV1 < 50% predicted) associated with chronic bronchitis and a history of frequent exacerbations (500 mcg once daily)"],
      ["Moderate to severe hepatic impairment (Child-Pugh Class B or C - black box contraindication)", "Hypersensitivity to roflumilast"],
      ["PSYCHIATRIC EVENTS: Increased risk of psychiatric adverse reactions including insomnia, anxiety, new or worsening depression, and suicidal ideation/behavior; assess mental health history before prescribing", "WEIGHT LOSS: Causes progressive, unexplained weight loss in up to 7-10% (monitor body weight at every visit; discontinue if unexplained significant weight loss occurs)", "NOT A BRONCHODILATOR: Do NOT use for the relief of acute bronchospasm", "Start with 250 mcg once daily for 4 weeks to reduce initial GI adverse effects (diarrhea, nausea)"],
      ["Diarrhoea (very common in first 4 weeks: up to 10-15%)", "Weight loss (mean loss 2-3 kg)", "Nausea", "Headache", "Insomnia", "Decreased appetite"],
      ["Suicidal ideation and completed suicide", "Severe depression / psychiatric disturbances", "Severe weight loss / cachexia", "Severe persistent diarrhea with dehydration"],
      ["Strong CYP inducers (rifampin, carbamazepine, phenobarbital - drastically reduce roflumilast exposure; avoid combination)", "Combined CYP3A4 and CYP1A2 inhibitors (erythromycin, fluvoxamine, ketoconazole - increase roflumilast levels and side effects)", "Theophylline (concurrent use not recommended due to additive PDE inhibition)"],
      ["Body weight at baseline and every visit (weigh patient regularly)", "Mental health status, mood changes, depression, or emergence of suicidal thoughts", "Frequency of moderate to severe COPD exacerbations"],
      "Category C; teratogenic in animal models; avoid during pregnancy.",
