      "Rapidly and completely absorbed from GI tract (bioavailability approx. 62%); peak plasma concentration in 1 hour; unaffected by food.",
      "Widely distributed into tissues; volume of distribution approx. 1 L/kg; 48% bound to plasma proteins.",
      "Extensively metabolized in the liver (approx. 90%) to inactive hydroxyethyltheophylline; minimal conversion to theophylline (<2%).",
      "Excreted in urine (approx. 50% as metabolites) and faeces; <4% excreted unchanged in urine.",
