      ["Maintenance treatment of bronchial asthma", "Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) with reversible bronchospasm", "Asthmatic bronchitis and chronic spastic bronchitis"],
      ["Known hypersensitivity to doxofylline or xanthines", "Acute myocardial infarction", "Severe hypotension", "Lactation"],
      ["Dramatically safer than theophylline, but use with caution in patients with severe cardiac disease, severe hypertension, or peptic ulcer disease", "Do not chew or crush tablets; take with water after meals", "No routine therapeutic drug monitoring (TDM) required at standard therapeutic doses (unlike theophylline)"],
      ["Nausea and vomiting", "Headache", "Epigastric pain / heartburn", "Dizziness", "Insomnia (much less frequent than theophylline)"],
      ["Cardiac arrhythmias / tachycardia (rare at therapeutic doses)", "Convulsions / seizures (only at extreme supratherapeutic overdoses)", "Severe hypotension"],
      ["Erythromycin, clarithromycin, ciprofloxacin (inhibit hepatic metabolism, increasing doxofylline levels)", "Cimetidine (increases doxofylline levels)", "Phenytoin, rifampin (induce clearance, reducing doxofylline levels)"],
      ["FEV1 and peak expiratory flow rates", "Heart rate and blood pressure", "Symptoms of dyspepsia or nausea"],
      "Category B/C; use during pregnancy only if potential benefit justifies potential risk.",
      "Strictly contraindicated during lactation; excreted in breast milk.",
      "Approved in children 6 years and older (syrup formulation: 6-12 mg/kg/day divided BID/TID).",
